"facebook":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/jackwhite"}],"homepage":[{"url":"http://jackwhiteiii.com/"}],"instagram":[{"url":"https://www.instagram.com/officialjackwhite/?hl=en"}],"musicbrainz":[{"id":"3ae2fb37-8a23-429d-9920-bac811c4fc22","url":"https://musicbrainz.org/artist/3ae2fb37-8a23-429d-9920-bac811c4fc22"}]},"upcomingEvents":{"tmr":6,"_total":44,"wts-tr":3,"_filtered":0,"ticketweb":1,"ticketmaster":34},"classifications":[{"type":{"id":"KZAyXgnZfZ7v7nI","name":"Undefined"},"genre":{"id":"KnvZfZ7vAeA","name":"Rock"},"family":false,"primary":true,"segment":{"id":"KZFzniwnSyZfZ7v7nJ","name":"Music"},"subType":{"id":"KZFzBErXgnZfZ7v7lJ","name":"Undefined"},"subGenre":{"id":"KZazBEonSMnZfZ7v6F1","name":"Pop"}}]}]},"nameOrigin":"custom","pleaseNote":"- Participants aged 14 and under are not admitted to the event. Participants under 18 may only enter accompanied by their parents (mother or father). However, participants who are legally under the responsibility of a guardian/custodian may enter with their legal guardian or custodian, provided that they document this status. - Participants of all ages are subject to ticketing. - Participants under 18 will be given wristbands in a different color. - Sale of alcohol and tobacco products to participants under 18 is prohibited. - Participants who exit the event area must purchase a new ticket to re-enter. - Please ensure that the wristband remains on your wrist throughout the festival. - Combined ticket holders will enter the event area on the second day using the wristband provided to them on the first day. - Pets are not allowed in the event venue. - The organizing company reserves the right to deny entry to individuals deemed inappropriate, provided that the ticket fee is refunded. - Open cigarette packs and tobacco will not be allowed in the venue. - Entry to the event area with firearms; flammable, explosive, or combustible items (*deodorants, sprays, perfumes, pepper spray, etc.); sharp, piercing, injuring objects; or any items that may be used for attack or defense, even if not intended as such (*helmets, camping chairs, selfie sticks, GoPro poles, tripods, chain accessories, etc.), as well as laser pointers, is prohibited. - The organizing company reserves the right to make any changes to the program due to unforeseen and unavoidable circumstances. - The organizing company reserves the right to change ticket prices. - Food and beverages may not be brought into the event area. - Food and beverages will be sold within the event area. - Entry with professional audio and visual equipment, video cameras, and photo cameras is prohibited. - Recording during the concert is strictly prohibited. The audience agrees that audio-visual recording devices may be confiscated. - Please keep your ticket and wristband throughout the concert. - All participants must carry their identification and present it upon request. - Participants must keep their personal belongings with them at all times. Responsibility for personal items lies with the participant. - There is no cloakroom or storage service in the festival area. - Security personnel will subject everyone entering the event area to a security check. - Sound systems in the event area may cause temporary hearing issues. - Lighting systems in the event area may cause temporary eye discomfort. - Concert tickets must be purchased only from official sales points designated by the organizer. The organizer reserves the right to remove holders of tickets not purchased from official sales points from the concert area. - Concert tickets are non-transferable and non-refundable. Lost tickets will not be reissued. - The right to use photographs and videos taken of attendees for promotional materials belongs to the organizer, and by attending the concert, participants accept this usage. - Bringing opened packages of tobacco and tobacco products into the event area is prohibited. - The event will take place under all weather conditions. Participants are advised to be prepared for all weather conditions. No ticket refunds will be issued.","description":"The City’s Escape Point: Babylon Soundgarden Taking place at Bonus Parkorman on August 22–23, Babylon Soundgarden is once again preparing to bring together music, nature, discovery, and shared experiences. Pozitif Müzik’s multi-layered festival culture continues to be one of the most distinctive gatherings of the summer, with its diverse stages, program that creates space for new discoveries, and atmosphere that lasts throughout the day. This year’s headliners, Jack White, TOMORA, and Wet Leg, reflect Babylon Soundgarden’s character of bringing together different musical worlds. Alternative rock icon Jack White, TOMORA—a collaboration uniting Norwegian artist AURORA and Tom Rowlands—and dynamic post-punk band Wet Leg are among the festival’s most anticipated performances. The festival’s first day, August 22, kicks off with an energetic lineup featuring TOMORA, Islandman, Vendredi Sur Mer, Rikas, and Lin Pesto. On August 23, Jack White, Wet Leg, The Kills, and Radio Free Alice will take the stage, bringing the festival’s momentum to its peak. Babylon’s platform dedicated to supporting the local scene, GLocals, continues to nurture a sense of discovery through emerging voices and independent productions. The festival taking place in Bonus Parkorman creates a sense of a brief escape from the city, while transforming into a powerful community built around music. Over two days spent in nature, Babylon Soundgarden offers not just a festival, but a summer experience lived together.","classifications":[{"genre":{"id":"KnvZfZ7vAvv","name":"Alternative"},"family":false,"segment":{"id":"KZFzniwnSyZfZ7v7nJ","name":"Music"}}]}	2026-07-15 18:02:58.837838	2026-07-15 18:02:58.837838
