ccess it, or if you did not purchase your ticket via membership, please contact Biletix Customer Services. - The organiser reserves the right to make changes to the terms and conditions for purchasing discounted tickets. - The organiser reserves the right to make changes to the venue and time of the event. - It is prohibited to bring food and drink into the event venue. - No spectators will be admitted to the venue once the event has started. - No cancellations, refunds or changes are permitted for purchased tickets. - It is prohibited to bring cameras or photographic equipment into the event venue.", "description": "Standing out as one of the most original and compelling voices in the UK jazz scene, Sarathy Korwar continues his productions as a drummer, composer, producer, and bandleader. His music fuses jazz, electronics, Indian folk, and classical influences, with a focus on decoloniality, community, race and transcendence. The musician’s latest album, There Is Beauty, There Already, released in the autumn of 2025, garnered praise from the global music press, as The Quietus magazine’s review included the words: “Showcasing the depths to which the drums can reach as instruments for ascension.” Sarathy Korwar Drum Ensemble will take the stage at Salon İKSV on September 29 as part of the 36th Akbank Jazz Festival, with the support of the Consulate General of India. Sarathy Korwar: Drums, tabla, electronics Magnus Mehta: Balophone, marimba, percussion Donna Thomson: Drums, electronics Prathap Ramchandran: Mridangam, ghatam, kanjira", "classifications": [{"genre": {"id": "KnvZfZ7vAvE", "name": "Jazz"}, "family": false, "segment": {"id": "KZFzniwnSyZfZ7v7nJ", "name": "Music"}}]}	2026-07-15 18:02:59.108551	2026-07-15 18:02:59.108551
