 systems in the event area may cause temporary hearing problems. - The stage lighting systems in the event area are harmful to people with MS and epilepsy; we kindly request that you take care. - The lighting systems in the event area may cause temporary eye discomfort. - Smoke and fog machines may be used in the event area. - Concert tickets must only be purchased from official sales points designated by the event organiser. The event organiser reserves the right to remove individuals from the concert venue if their tickets were not purchased from official sales points. - Spectators entering the event venue must purchase a new ticket if they leave the venue. - The event organiser reserves the right to use photographs and videos taken by concert attendees in promotional materials. By attending the concert, participants agree to this right. - As barcode/ticket checks will be carried out upon entry, you must present your ticket. If your ticket was purchased with a membership, you can access your ticket from the \\\\"My Tickets\\\\" section after logging in. If you are unable to access it, or if you did not purchase your ticket with a membership, please contact Biletix Customer Services.", "description": "On September 26, 2026, Babylon welcomes Amsterdam-based rising pop artist Isabel van Gelder! At just 23 years old, Isabel van Gelder has already made a remarkable breakthrough. With her angelic vocals and captivating stage presence, she stands out as one of the most compelling new voices in contemporary pop. Her emotionally layered storytelling ballads are balanced by carefree, upbeat tracks, as she effortlessly blends dreamy melodies with deeply personal lyrics. Following the release of her singles “Die For You” and “My Silly Boy,” Isabel quickly captured widespread attention, amassing millions of views on Instagram and TikTok. Her debut EP Minor Details has reached millions of streams on Spotify, and her first European tour sold out within weeks. Now, she returns with a newly expanded European tour, featuring larger venues and many more cities. No longer a “hidden gem,” Isabel van Gelder is ready to take the stage at Babylon on September 26, 2026, for an unforgettable night.", "classifications": [{"genre": {"id": "KnvZfZ7vAev", "name": "Pop"}, "family": false, "segment": {"id": "KZFzniwnSyZfZ7v7nJ", "name": "Music"}, "subGenre": {"id": "KZazBEonSMnZfZ7vkIk", "name": "Singer-Songwriter"}}]}	2026-07-15 18:02:59.108551	2026-07-15 18:02:59.108551
