any person deemed unsuitable or likely to disturb other guests, subject to a refund of the ticket price. - Guests must adhere to the specified seating arrangement. Guests are required to remain in their designated seats throughout the event. - We kindly request that you arrive at the event entrance with your ticket at least 30 minutes before the start time. - As a barcode/ticket check will be carried out upon entry, you must present your ticket. If your ticket was purchased via membership, please log in to your account and access your ticket via the 'My Tickets' section. If you are unable to access it, or if you did not purchase your ticket via membership, please contact Biletix Customer Services. - The organiser reserves the right to make changes to the terms and conditions for purchasing discounted tickets. - The organiser reserves the right to make changes to the venue and time of the event. - It is prohibited to bring food and drink into the event venue. - No spectators will be admitted to the venue once the event has started. - No cancellations, refunds or changes are permitted for purchased tickets. - It is prohibited to bring cameras or photographic equipment into the event venue.", "description": "“Music and life do not separate” says saxophone virtuoso James Carter, “my elders have taught me that music is a culture and a way of life.” Grown up with the recordings of Billie Holiday and Ella Fitzgerald and having shared a stage with Wynton Marsalis at a young age, the musician has been among the most celebrated jazz figures of his generation, known for a high-energy musical approach that traverses tenor, alto, and soprano saxophones. Having released numerous recordings to date under labels like Blue Note, EmArcy, and Atlantic, James Carter will be a guest of the 36th Akbank Jazz Festival with a concert at the Zorlu PSM Turkcell Platinum Stage on October 3, as part of the Coltrane: A Centennial Supreme tour. Carter summarizes this special performance in the spirit of celebrating the centennial of maestro Coltrane’s birth as follows: “I think it’s essential that we really focus on not just the overwhelming catalog of Coltrane’s musical output, but also on the spirit that brought these documents forth. It is our number one objective in this group to celebrate and [...] to join his spirit in these performances for you.” James Carter: Saxophones Gerard Gibbs: Piano Hilliard Greene: Bass Alex White: Drums", "classifications": [{"genre": {"id": "KnvZfZ7vAvE", "name": "Jazz"}, "family": false, "segment": {"id": "KZFzniwnSyZfZ7v7nJ", "name": "Music"}, "subGenre": {"id": "KZazBEonSMnZfZ7vkda", "name": "Jazz"}}]}	2026-07-15 18:02:59.108551	2026-07-15 18:02:59.108551
