cket check will be carried out upon entry, you must present your ticket. If your ticket was purchased via membership, please log in to your account and access your ticket via the 'My Tickets' section. If you are unable to access it, or if you did not purchase your ticket via membership, please contact Biletix Customer Services. - The organiser reserves the right to make changes to the terms and conditions for purchasing discounted tickets. - The organiser reserves the right to make changes to the venue and time of the event. - It is prohibited to bring food and drink into the event venue. - No spectators will be admitted to the venue once the event has started. - No cancellations, refunds or changes are permitted for purchased tickets. - It is prohibited to bring cameras or photographic equipment into the event venue.", "description": "A keyboardist, producer, songwriter and bandleader based in South London, Joe Armon-Jones is an alumnus of the education programme Tomorrow’s Warriors and a founding member of Ezra Collective. His virtuoso piano playing and improvisatory talents have made him a sought-after collaborator. After releasing two solo albums on Gilles Peterson’s Brownswood Recordings, Armon-Jones launched his own record label, Aquarii Records, and collaborated with dubstep pioneer Mala and his long-term creative partner Maxwell Owin on club-ready link-ups. In 2025, he embarked on his biggest creative project yet–the two-part opus All The Quiet. These two distinct but conceptually linked albums expanded his sound into new musical and sonic realms, assisted by a wealth of special guests including Asheber, Greentea Peng, Wu Lu, Hak Baker and Yazmin Lacey. Joe Armon-Jones will perform at Frankhan Selectist on September 26th as part of the 36th Akbank Jazz Festival.", "classifications": [{"genre": {"id": "KnvZfZ7vAvE", "name": "Jazz"}, "family": false, "segment": {"id": "KZFzniwnSyZfZ7v7nJ", "name": "Music"}, "subGenre": {"id": "KZazBEonSMnZfZ7vkda", "name": "Ja