"Performer"}, "subGenre": {"id": "KZazBEonSMnZfZ7vkIk", "name": "Singer-Songwriter"}}]}]}, "nameOrigin": "custom", "pleaseNote": "- The event organiser reserves the right to refuse entry to the venue to any person deemed unsuitable or likely to disturb other guests, subject to a refund of the ticket price. - Guests must adhere to the specified seating arrangement. Guests are required to remain in their designated seats throughout the event. - We kindly request that you arrive at the event entrance with your ticket at least 30 minutes before the start time. - As a barcode/ticket check will be carried out upon entry, you must present your ticket. If your ticket was purchased via membership, please log in to your account and access your ticket via the 'My Tickets' section. If you are unable to access it, or if you did not purchase your ticket via membership, please contact Biletix Customer Services. - The organiser reserves the right to make changes to the terms and conditions for purchasing discounted tickets. - The organiser reserves the right to make changes to the venue and time of the event. - It is prohibited to bring food and drink into the event venue. - No spectators will be admitted to the venue once the event has started. - No cancellations, refunds or changes are permitted for purchased tickets. - It is prohibited to bring cameras or photographic equipment into the event venue.", "description": "Momoko is one of the UK electronic and jazz scene’s best-kept secrets. A self-taught drummer, producer, songwriter, and vocalist, she has brought her unique touch to collaborations with Alabaster DePlume, Matthew Herbert, Coby Sey, Tirzah, and Nadeem Din-Gabisi. Extensive touring behind the drum kit, at the keys and in front of the mic have honed her compositional and production instincts. Her debut solo albüm Momoko, released under the Strut label in February 2026, underscores that she is a composer and performer who rejects imitation, sculpting her sound through f